# Expense Tracker Project

React + Vite expense tracker starter. Keep changes focused and match existing patterns.

## Stack

- React 19 with functional components and hooks
- Vite 7 (ES modules, `npm run dev` on port 5173)
- Plain JavaScript/JSX — no TypeScript unless explicitly requested
- Component styles in colocated `.css` files (e.g. `App.css`)

## Project Structure

```
src/
  main.jsx    # entry point
  App.jsx     # main app component
  App.css     # app styles
  index.css   # global styles
```

## Domain Model

Transactions have: `id`, `description`, `amount`, `type` (`"income"` | `"expense"`), `category`, `date`.

Categories: `food`, `housing`, `utilities`, `transport`, `entertainment`, `salary`, `other`.

## Coding Conventions

- Use `useState` for local state; extract custom hooks only when logic is reused
- Prefer minimal, readable diffs over large refactors
- Match existing naming: camelCase for variables/functions, kebab-case for CSS classes
- Run `npm run lint` after substantive changes

## Known Starter Issues

This is a course starter with intentional bugs and rough UI. When fixing:

- `amount` is stored as a string — coerce to number before math (`Number()` or `parseFloat()`)
- Verify income/expense totals and balance calculations after changes
- Improve UI incrementally; keep the app functional at each step

## What to Avoid

- Adding dependencies without a clear need
- Converting to TypeScript or adding a backend unless asked
- Over-abstracting (no premature component splits or utility libraries)
- Creating commits unless the user explicitly requests them
